Mark 12 comes from an obscenely large horde of barbarians.   I started
numbering them about a month ago to document my frustration.  At least
3 had their full AK before doing something totally stupid (drowning,
choking, etc).  My wife has been looking at me like I'm nuts when I
come to bed fuming at the latest YASD.

Mark 12 had a somewhat easy first few levels with a potion shop on 2,
general on 3 and hardware on 4.   The mines were on level 2 and the
minetown altar was co-aligned. I finished Sokoban before completing
the mines. Converted an altar on 4 and received Cleaver, Mojo and
Giantslayer from saccing.

On the Oracle level, I received a fountain wish (Grey DSM) while
dipping some potions. I later returned to the Oracle level to find a
convenient room to rev. genocide nurses for dancing up 61 hp.  Sokoban
gave me the bag of holding and Demonbane (stashed it) from an Angel.

Level 10 had a lawful temple (for protection) and I converted the
chaotic altar.  Sacced some more to get Vorpy and Ogremasher.  I also
got crowned at this point (although I think it was on a return trip as
opposed to the original downwards drive).  For most of the game, I
alternated between using Mojo, Vorpy and Ogremasher (in the quest).

Level 12 was the big room (oval shaped).  With invisibility, I danced
around and took out the monsters individually.  Level 13 had the
portal to Fort Ludios.  I started it but I still did not have
reflection, so I regrouped and returned later.   I used mostly Vorpy
for the fun/style of beheading.
Level 14 had the quest portal, a Chaotic (converted to neutral) altar
and a general store.  I started the quest but I went back to the
regular dungeon to tame a dog  in order to get rid of the troll
corpses (annoying),   I used Ogremasher on the ogres because it just
seems like the apporpriate thing to do and my skill level slot was
already expert for Mojo.

Level 15 had a graveyard (no wraith corpse) and level 16 had a throne
room.   Level 18 rminded me of university days in the mid 80s when I
played Rogue too much.  Level 19 had a bee hive...yum, yum.   Level 20
had yet another temple (Neutral). I got Telportisis from a Tengu and
MagicBane (never used) from a sac. Level 21 had a Lawful temple and
level 23 a chaotic temple. 

Medusa (level 24) went down really easy. and there was a previous Mark
Barbarian bones pile on level 25.

The castle went down easy with conflict.   I found a pair of GoP and a
hawaiian shirt in the armoury.  Wished for MM, speed boots and a helm
of telepathy (forgot to ask rustproof!!).  I think all the other
wishes went for more MM.  I wrote many, many scrolls of identify,
enchant armour and enchant weapon.

Level 36 was Baalzebub (?) and the stairs to Vlad.  I found Firebrand
in Vlad's tower which I used on the astral planes.  Level 39 was
Orcus, it was a chase and fight marathon. I was worried at one point
when I was surrounded with monsters including a Green Slime.  There
seemed to be many more Green Slime than in my usual games.  I have
never been slimed, but I am weary.

VB was on 49.  Moloch's sanctum was hack/slash the bugs and remove
curse.  I played wreckless by ESCing the long, long list of messages
(because of conflict), but the full moon shined on me and no unseen
message came back to haunt me.  The climb back up was hindered by 11
mysterious throw backs.

On the Elemental planes, I zipped through quite effortless.  Even Air
was easy with on 2 Air engulfings.  Water just took a while find the
&*^%$^%$ portal as all the ;s were genocided.

On the Astral plane, I started left, but that was famine and chaotic.
So I went up the middle with pestilence (uni-horned and full healing)
for the correct Altar.  I called my Invisible Guardian Angel and Offer
the Amulet...

An invisible choir sings, and you are bathed in radiance...

The voice of Crom booms: "Congratulations, mortal!"
"In return for thy service, I grant thee the gift of Immortality!"
You ascend to the status of Demigod...

